# Python safepoint slice 2 (recursion): report

Slice 2 is implemented, and the Node and Dart lanes passed in full. On the JVM, every namespace that touches this slice passed. One JVM group is not confirmed: the `yin.repl.*` tests with `yin.vm-test` and `yin.repl-test`, which this slice doesn't touch. It was still running when I wrote this. Nothing is staged or committed.

## What was built
- **One dynamic-context record.** `py.rt/handlers` is replaced by one cell, `py.rt/ctx`, holding `{:handlers :depth :frame}`. `py/try`, `py/try-finally` and `py/call-ec` save the whole record and restore it whole on re-entry or escape, so depth goes back to its value at capture rather than being decremented.
  - Each handler frame now also records the depth it was pushed at, and a `finally` block runs at that depth while an exception unwinds.
  - `:frame` is always nil for now; it is reserved for tracing.
  - Generators save and restore the whole record at each crossing.
- **Depth counting.** The stage now has an exit kind: at every `:call` site the `:return` hook is applied to the body's value, so it runs only on normal exit. It is still an ordinary `:application` row, with no new tag.
  - `py.sp/call` polls for signals, then adds one to the depth. If the depth would go over the limit it raises `RecursionError` through `py/raise`.
  - `py.sp/return` subtracts one and passes the value through.
  - The no-op hooks gained `py.sp/return` as identity.
- **`RecursionError`** is a builtin class in the base prelude, under `RuntimeError` as in CPython, so it is still under `Exception`.
- **Recursion limit.** The limit lives in the cell `py.sp/limit`, default 1000. `py.sp/set-recursion-limit!` accepts an int of at least 1; 0 or less raises `ValueError` and a non-int raises `TypeError`. `py.sp/recursion-limit` reads it back.
- **`sys.setrecursionlimit` and `sys.settrace` are refused.** The lowering rejects every `import` ("Unsupported Python construct: import"), so `sys` can't be reached from Python, and a test now pins that.
  - Slice 1 never had an explicit settrace error; the import refusal is the behavior that remains.
  - A composition can set the limit through `py.sp/set-recursion-limit!`, the same way signal handlers are registered through `py.sp/set-handler!`.

